{{!-- The rows of one guidance group: a name, an "optional" tag where the step can be skipped,
      and the gloss.

      Here rather than inline because the list around it comes in two flavours — numbered where
      the order is the point (the write-up steps), plain everywhere else — and the rows were
      written out identically inside each branch. Two copies of one <li> means any change to a
      guidance row is two edits, and the missed one is invisible: only the write-up section takes
      the ordered branch, so an edit made to the <ul> copy alone looks correct everywhere a reader
      is likely to check.

      Invoked with the group's `items`, so `this` is the row list; the shared "optional" tag is
      passed in as `optionalLabel`. NOT reached for through `@root`, which would tie a partial
      named for every GM-prep kind to one tab's context shape: rendered from the Sites or Hazards
      tab, a page sheet or the canvas overlay — all of which the generic name invites, and reuse is
      why it was extracted — every optional row would emit an empty <em> with no error to say so.

      Context: the group's item rows ({name, optional, gloss}), plus
        optionalLabel  the localized "optional" tag --}}
{{#each this}}
<li><strong>{{name}}</strong>{{#if optional}} <em class="steading-threats-guide-optional">{{../optionalLabel}}</em>{{/if}}<span>{{gloss}}</span></li>
{{/each}}
